 (uint64), Dev (uint64), Ino (uint64), Blocks (int64), Blksize (int64), ModTime (time.Time), and the underlying os.FileInfo for compatibility with os package functions.\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement Stat(path string) (*FileInfo, error) and Lstat(path string) (*FileInfo, error) that call os.Stat/os.Lstat and extract extended fields from the underlying syscall.Stat_t via a platform-specific extraction function. Per prd002-sys R2.1.\"\n      - id: R5\n        text: \"Abstract the Darwin/Linux divergence in syscall.Stat_t field names using build-tagged source files: st_mtimespec on Darwin vs st_mtim on Linux, and platform-specific st_blocks interpretation. Per prd002-sys R2.3.\"\n      - id: R6\n        text: \"Implement InstallSIGPIPEHandler() that installs a signal handler calling os.Exit(0) on SIGPIPE. Must not use signal.Ignore; must install a handler so deferred cleanup functions do not run, matching GNU behavior. Per prd002-sys R3.1-R3.2.\"\n      - id: R7\n        text: \"Implement OnTerminalResize(callback func(width int)) that registers a SIGWINCH handler. When the terminal is resized, the handler calls TerminalWidth() and invokes the callback with the new width. Must support multiple calls to OnTerminalResize; each registered callback must be called on resize. Per prd002-sys R4.1-R4.2.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use golang.org/x/sys/unix for TIOCGWINSZ ioctl. Must not shell out to tput or stty. Must not import golang.org/x/term. Per prd002-sys R1.3.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use Go build tags (//go:build darwin and //go:build linux) for platform-specific stat field extraction. fileinfo.go defines the FileInfo struct and Stat/Lstat functions which call a platform-specific extractStatFields function defined in stat_darwin.go and stat_linux.go. Per prd002-sys R2.3.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"InstallSIGPIPEHandler must install a signal handler that calls os.Exit(0) on SIGPIPE so deferred cleanup functions do not run, matching GNU behavior where SIGPIPE terminates silently. Must not use signal.Ignore. Per prd002-sys R3.2.\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Lstat on a symlink must return the symlink's own st_mode with type bits showing symlink, not the target's mode. Per prd002-sys AC3.\"\n      - id: D5\n        text: \"No cgo dependency. All syscall access uses golang.org/x/sys/unix which provides pure-Go implementations. Must compile on both darwin/arm64 and linux/amd64 with no cgo. Per prd002-sys AC5.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"TerminalWidth() compiles and returns (int, error). When stdout is not a terminal, it returns a non-nil error. Per prd002-sys AC1.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Stat() and Lstat() return *FileInfo with correct Nlink, Uid, Gid, Dev, Ino, Blocks, Blksize, Rdev, Mode, Size, and ModTime fields populated from syscall.Stat_t. Per prd002-sys AC2.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Lstat() on a symlink returns FileInfo with Mode type bits showing symlink, not the target's mode. Per prd002-sys AC3.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"InstallSIGPIPEHandler() registers a handler that calls os.Exit(0) when SIGPIPE is received. Per prd002-sys AC4.\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"OnTerminalResize registers callbacks that are invoked with the new terminal width when SIGWINCH is received. Multiple callbacks can be registered via successive calls. Per prd002-sys R4.1-R4.2.\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"All pkg/sys code compiles on both darwin/arm64 and linux/amd64 with no build errors and no cgo. Per prd002-sys AC5.\"\n      - id: AC7\n        text: \"All pkg/sys code compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint. Per prd002-sys AC6.\"\n```","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"8ad748e0-6dd7-472e-9537-1f51e5854752","total_cost_usd":0.996632,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":123072,"cache_read_input_tokens":15594,"output_tokens":8785,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":123072,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":8785,"cacheReadInputTokens":15594,"cacheCreationInputTokens":123072,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.996632,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"uuid":"efaf6579-328a-43f7-93ab-4f9594c66e81"}
